From 596c604bf727503c875a5ee7d789b43bcbca9909 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:26:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix #18: glk_set_echo_line_event() no longer affects a
 pending line input request

The Glk spec says glk_set_echo_line_event() "does not affect a pending
line input request", but handle_line_input read the window's current echo
setting. Record the echo setting when line input is requested and use
that when the input arrives or the request is cancelled.

Add echolinetest, a small Glulx test (Inform 6 source included) that
changes the echo setting while a line request is pending in both
directions.
---
 remglk/src/glkapi/mod.rs       |   4 ++-
 remglk/src/glkapi/windows.rs   |   2 ++
 tests/echolinetest.inf         |  59 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/echolinetest.ulx         | Bin 0 -> 2048 bytes
 tests/echolinetest.ulx.regtest |  17 ++++++++++
 tests/runtests.sh              |   2 ++
 6 files changed, 83 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/echolinetest.inf
 create mode 100644 tests/echolinetest.ulx
 create mode 100644 tests/echolinetest.ulx.regtest

